1
00:00:00,298 --> 00:00:09,528
(Q11（单选）) Hello and welcome. My name’s Heather McCallum and I’m one of the potters who work here at Edelman Pottery.

2
00:00:09,528 --> 00:00:15,848
Before we go into the workshop, I just want to say a bit about the craft of pottery.

3
00:00:15,848 --> 00:00:21,984
Then we’ll have a look at the equipment, and you can try making a pot of your own.

4
00:00:21,984 --> 00:00:35,652
[Q11干扰项（B） many people 只是知道，不是practise] Like many people, I’m sure you know that pottery as an art form is tens of thousands of years old, and we know this because it stands the test of time.

5
00:00:35,652 --> 00:00:42,981
[Q11答案句（A） ：survive = last 平行替换， not ... in the same way ... do 表示比较longer ， earth =in the ground] Things like baskets and pictures don’t survive in the earth in the same way that pots do.

6
00:00:42,981 --> 00:00:52,063
[Q11干扰项（C） 变成碎片 不一定等于 can be repaired easily,不要过多联想] And even if ancient pots are found in small pieces, they still provide a lot of information about the past.

7
00:00:52,063 --> 00:01:01,832
(Q12) There’s no doubt that pottery has given archaeologists a fascinating insight into how ancient humans lived.

8
00:01:01,832 --> 00:01:23,760
[Q12干扰项C： 否定-语义- lost， Q12答案句B： impression n.压痕= mark, tell = identify ,] The shape of an artefact may have been lost, but archaeologists can tell whether the pots were for, say, storage or cooking by examining the impressions on the clay, the scratches from tools; and the clay itself can reveal where the pots came from.

9
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:32,551
(Q13) When I ask people why they want to take a pottery class with me, they sometimes talk about these things.

10
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:50,325
[Q13答案句（C）hope = want to, last longer than they do = outlive + Q13干扰项（B） 否定 -语义 不管是否good] Like our ancestors, they hope that something they create will also last longer than they do, that their work – whether it is good or not – might say something about humanity many years after their death.

11
00:01:50,325 --> 00:01:55,250
(Q14) Of course, you will all have your own reasons for coming here.

12
00:01:55,250 --> 00:02:08,512
[Q14答案句（A）  what i love most = value most,   calming effect] As far as I’m concerned, what I love most is the concentration you need to make a good pot. That focus takes you away from the stresses of everyday life.

13
00:02:08,512 --> 00:02:21,493
[Q 14干扰项BC， 主体不同] If you’re elderly, it’s also good exercise for hands and wrists and helps with arthritis and, of course, it’s a fun activity for children because it’s so messy!

14
00:02:21,493 --> 00:02:33,786
(Q15) [Q干扰项C/A。 C：仅提及， 不符合 quickly，   A gift for friends 不是 join courses] Here at Edelman Pottery, we show you some of the basic pottery techniques so that you can use these to create whatever you wish – a gift for a friend, perhaps.

15
00:02:33,786 --> 00:02:43,569
[Q15答案句（B）nearly everyone= most of the visitor, first time = never] Like nearly everyone who comes here, I’m sure this is the first time you will have tried the art, so we’ll keep things simple today.

16
00:02:43,569 --> 00:02:49,569
(Q16) Now, before we move on, can I just say a word about what you’re wearing.

17
00:02:49,569 --> 00:02:58,990
[Q16答案句（C） remove = take off] As we said in our email, please remove any watches, necklaces, etc. and put them somewhere safe.

18
00:02:58,990 --> 00:03:12,971
[Q16干扰项A： apron不是一定要put on] If you have long hair, do tie it back now. We’ll provide aprons later, but I trust your clothes are old but comfortable – not your favourite T-shirt or jeans!

19
00:03:12,971 --> 00:03:19,788
(Q17&18（多选）) [陶窑与烧制] So now we’re in the workshop. Have a look around – there’s a lot going on.

20
00:03:19,788 --> 00:03:32,366
To make pottery that will last, you need a potter’s wheel, a kiln – which is basically a very hot oven where you fire the pottery – and some tools.

21
00:03:32,366 --> 00:03:40,828
So first, the kiln. If you look over in the far corner, you’ll see one of ours.

22
00:03:40,828 --> 00:03:51,324
Since their invention, kilns have changed very little, though in the past 20 years, a lot of progress has been made in temperature control.

23
00:03:51,324 --> 00:04:05,822
Basically, a kiln removes the water from clay at temperatures of around a thousand degrees Celsius. This allows anything you’ve made to set permanently in shape.

24
00:04:05,822 --> 00:04:14,233
It’s a pretty ugly, heavy object that’s hard to keep in a house or flat so most people don’t have one.

25
00:04:14,233 --> 00:04:28,860
You may think, ‘Can’t I use my oven?’ Well, that’s possible but domestic ovens don’t really get hot enough and eventually the clay will crack and fall apart.

26
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:38,288
Some people fire pottery in a fire pit outside – but bear in mind that can be dangerous.

27
00:04:38,288 --> 00:04:46,680
You also need to know about safety procedures for kilns as they release toxic compounds into the air.

28
00:04:46,680 --> 00:05:01,432
[陶轮与工具] Every potter needs a potter’s wheel. This machine is used to shape the clay into an object with circular walls or sides – such as a bowl.

29
00:05:01,432 --> 00:05:10,851
Its invention revolutionised the pottery industry, allowing multiple items to be produced in a day.

30
00:05:10,851 --> 00:05:18,899
Lastly, there are a number of different tools that potters use, depending on what they want to make.

31
00:05:18,899 --> 00:05:26,771
When you start, your hands can make all kinds of shapes and curves without relying on a sculpting tool.

32
00:05:26,771 --> 00:05:42,064
However, there are some basic tools that you will need to handle the clay on the wheel. Some look very strange and have even odder names that you may find hard to remember.

33
00:05:42,064 --> 00:05:54,862
Rather than go through them all now, I’ll just name a few tools as we go along. We can provide these and I wouldn’t recommend spending money on them yet.

34
00:05:54,862 --> 00:05:57,362
So let’s try making a pot of your own …

